      "bio_summary": {
        "value": "Tim Kennedy grew up in a working class family in Buffalo – he’s one of us. From an early age, he has always been driven to help people – it’s why he started his career as an occupational therapist, and it’s what led him to public service. In the House of Representatives, Tim has stood up for Western New York values. After being elected in a 2024 Special Election and re-elected to a full term months later, Tim was appointed to the House Committee for Veterans Affairs and the House Committee on Homeland Security, where he serves as the Ranking Member of the Subcommittee on Emergency Management and Technology.",
